@page "/"
@using GSBC.Accounting.WASM.Features.Expenses
@inject DraftSession Session

<PageTitle>GSBC Finance Forms</PageTitle>

@*
    The landing page: the two forms, and the way back into anything already started.

    The drafts card is third rather than first on purpose. Most people arriving here are starting a
    form, not resuming one, and a list they have no entries in would be the first thing they read.

    IT IS ALSO ABSENT ENTIRELY UNTIL THE BROWSER HAS A SESSION. Nothing on this client can read the
    __gsbc_anon cookie - it is HttpOnly - so DraftSession asks the server, and until it answers there is
    no honest way to offer somebody "your saved drafts": the link would lead to a list the server
    refuses to talk about. A first-time visitor sees the two forms and nothing else.
*@

<div class="layout norail">
    <main>
        <p class="lede">
            Two forms, and a person at the end of both. A submission here is <strong>not</strong> a
            ledger entry &mdash; it collects the claim, its receipts and its declarations so a
            reviewer can check them and file the result in Xero.
        </p>

        <section class="card">
            <header>
                <span class="num">01</span>
                <h3>Church Debit Card Purchase</h3>
                <span class="hint">One form per card transaction</span>
            </header>
            <div class="body">
                <p class="help">
                    For a purchase already charged to a church debit card. Needs the cardholder, the
                    transaction, an itemised receipt, and the split between church and personal spend.
                </p>
                @* cardlink is a mobile affordance and does nothing on a desktop width. A bare text
                   link is a ~20px tap target, and this is the only way into either form. *@
                <p><a class="cardlink" href="/forms/debit-card-purchase">Open the debit card form</a></p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="card">
            <header>
                <span class="num">02</span>
                <h3>Expense Reimbursement</h3>
                <span class="hint">One line per receipt</span>
            </header>
            <div class="body">
                <p class="help">
                    For money you spent yourself and want back. Needs your contact and payment
                    details, the expense period, and a receipt behind every line.
                </p>
                <p><a class="cardlink" href="/forms/expense-reimbursement">Open the reimbursement form</a></p>
            </div>
        </section>


        @if (Session.HasSession)
        {
            <section class="card">
                <header>
                    <span class="num">&mdash;</span>
                    <h3>Your saved drafts</h3>
                    <span class="hint">Kept for this browser</span>
                </header>
                <div class="body">
                    <p class="help">
                        Both forms save themselves as you fill them in, so you can close the page and come
                        back later. Drafts are kept for the browser you started them on &mdash; clearing
                        your cookies, or switching to another device, loses them &mdash; and a draft nobody
                        edits is deleted after 90 days.
                    </p>
                    <p><a class="cardlink" href="/drafts">See your saved drafts</a></p>
                </div>
            </section>
        }

        <p class="footnote">
            Neither form asks you to sign in, and neither is a substitute for approval. Sections 7 and
            8 of each &mdash; independent approval, and finance use &mdash; are completed after you
            submit, by somebody who is not you.
        </p>
    </main>
</div>

@code
{
    [CascadingParameter] private MainLayout Layout { get; set; } = default!;

    protected override void OnInitialized() => Layout.SetTitle("Finance Forms");

    // The card appears on the second render, once the server has said whether this browser owns
    // anything. Deliberately silent on failure: this page has nothing to tell somebody about drafts if
    // it cannot find out, and a banner here would be about the plumbing rather than about their form.
    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        try
        {
            await Session.DraftsAsync();
        }
        catch
        {
            // Unreachable server. Leaves the card hidden, which is the same answer as no session.
        }
    }

}
